  "solution": {
    "text": "The benzene ring to which &gt;NH group is directly attached is activated for the attack of <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math> as –NH group is highly ringh activating due to +R effect. the ring to which <math><msubsup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">ƒ</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">‚</mi></mrow></msubsup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></math> group is directly attached is deactivated towards electrophillic substitution. As <math><msubsup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">ƒ</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">‚</mi></mrow></msubsup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></math> group is ring deactivating due to –R effect in addition the <math><msubsup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">ƒ</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">‚</mi></mrow></msubsup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></math> group is ortho-para directing but para position is favourable for the attach of <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math> . Hence the product formed is as follows<br /><img alt=\"New1.15.PNG\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/b7466ac0-1bf9-47c0-9719-f4ec8ab.png\" style=\"width: 400px; height: 126px;\" />",
